 "488": {
  "action": "confirm",
  "canonical": "Design data encodings for both forward compatibility (old code can read data written by new code) and backward compatibility (new code can read data written by old code), because both are needed to roll out upgrades to different parts of a system independently; when older code reads, updates, and rewrites a record, preserve unknown fields, and remember data outlives code \u2014 it persists for years in its original encoding while application versions are replaced in minutes."
 },
