 "531": {
  "action": "confirm",
  "canonical": "Do not build distributed coordination or consensus yourself \u2014 two-phase commit and consensus algorithms like Paxos are notoriously hard to implement correctly \u2014 but use a proven coordination service such as ZooKeeper, Consul, or etcd (which run a small fixed quorum voting among themselves while serving many clients) for small, slow-changing coordination data such as which node leads a partition, not for fast-changing application state; note that service discovery alone does not require consensus (DNS suffices)."
